### ThermoGrid demo requests (VS Code "REST Client" / IntelliJ HTTP Client). Plan phase 10.
### No secret is stored in this file: passwords come from your environment (SEED_*_PASSWORD from .env).
### Change @gateway if you set GATEWAY_PORT (for example http://localhost:18080).
@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@viewerPassword = {{$processEnv SEED_VIEWER_PASSWORD}}
@operatorPassword = {{$processEnv SEED_OPERATOR_PASSWORD}}
@adminPassword = {{$processEnv SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}

### 1. Login as ADMIN (token used by the requests below)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.token}}

### 2. Who am I
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3. Topology (4 zones, 16 racks)
GET {{gateway}}/api/topology
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 4. Seed the demo workloads (ADMIN)
POST {{gateway}}/api/workloads/seed-demo
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5. Latest rack telemetry
GET {{gateway}}/api/telemetry/racks/latest
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6. Active alerts
GET {{gateway}}/api/alerts?state=ACTIVE&limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7. Submit a workload (OPERATOR or ADMIN)
POST {{gateway}}/api/workloads
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "batch-etl-demo", "cpuDemand": 30, "priority": "LOW" }

### 8. Scheduler status and recent decisions
GET {{gateway}}/api/scheduler/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/scheduler/decisions?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 9. Cooling units
GET {{gateway}}/api/cooling/units
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 10. Scenario 2: degrade cooling in Z2 (efficiency 0.15, see decision D-093)
POST {{gateway}}/api/sim/failures
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "COOLING_DEGRADED", "targetId": "Z2", "param": 0.15, "durationSec": 0 }

### 11. Active failures (copy an id for the DELETE below)
GET {{gateway}}/api/sim/failures?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 12. Clear a failure (replace 1 with the id from step 11)
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/sim/failures/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 13. Scenario 6: fail the Z3 cooling unit
POST {{gateway}}/api/sim/failures
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "COOLING_FAILURE", "targetId": "Z3", "durationSec": 0 }

### 14. Platform status (which services are UP)
GET {{gateway}}/api/platform/services
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 15. Reset the simulation between runs (ADMIN)
POST {{gateway}}/api/sim/control
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "RESET" }

### --- Security demonstrations ---

### S-01 No token -> 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/topology

### S-03 VIEWER cannot submit -> 403 (login first, then the POST)
# @name loginViewer
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "viewer", "password": "{{viewerPassword}}" }

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/workloads
Authorization: Bearer {{loginViewer.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "denied", "cpuDemand": 10, "priority": "LOW" }

### S-07 /internal is never routed by the gateway -> 404
GET {{gateway}}/internal/topology
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
